The??operator returns the right operand when the left operand isnullish(nullorundefined),
otherwise it returns the left operand.

When programming, a lot of values can befalsey(like 0, empty strings, false,
undefined, null, NaN).

However, sometimes you want to check if a variable isnullish(eitherundefinedornull),
like when it is okay for a variable to be an empty string, or a false value.
Then you can use thenullish coalescing operator.

??is an ES2020 feature.

ES2020is fully supported in all modern browsers sinceSeptember 2020:

### Code Snippets

```
let x = 6;
let y = 3;
let z = (x < 10 && y > 1)

---

let x = 6;
let y = -3;
let z = (x > 0 || y > 0)

---

let x = (5 == 8);
let y = !(5 == 8)

---

let name = null;
let text = "missing";
let result = name ?? text;
